<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  com.aiteamforge.host-ready.plist — TEMPLATE (XACA-1066)

  Canonical source:  scripts/templates/host-ready-plist.template   (dev-team)
  Tap mirror:        share/templates/kanban/host-ready-plist.template
  Rendered by:       _render_launchagent_template() in
                      homebrew-tap/libexec/lib/launchagents.sh — the SAME
                      renderer as this directory's other siblings
                      (backup-plist.template, lcars-health-plist.template).
                      No new sed placeholder was added for this template;
                      every placeholder below is already resolved by that
                      (Token names appear WITHOUT the doubled braces on
                      purpose: a "no surviving placeholder" render gate --
                      the follow-up this ticket flags as missing -- would
                      otherwise match this comment and fail on a correctly
                      rendered plist.)
                      renderer's existing chain (USER_HOME, HOME_DIR,
                      AITEAMFORGE_DIR, LOG_DIR, ...). The script path is
                      composed from the AITEAMFORGE_DIR placeholder rather than a new
                      HOST_READY_SCRIPT token, the same way the renderer
                      already composes the AUTO_UPGRADE_SCRIPT sibling path.
  Design doc:         kanban/plans/XACA-1066/XACA-1066-001-design.md §7

  ── WHY THIS FILE'S PROVENANCE DIVERGES FROM ITS share/templates/kanban/
     SIBLINGS — DO NOT "FIX" THIS BACK ───────────────────────────────────
  backup-plist.template, lcars-health-plist.template and
  cr-confluence-poller-plist.template are TAP-NATIVE: they have no dev-team
  canonical source and no sync-tap.sh entry (verified — grep for their
  basenames in sync-tap.sh returns nothing). This file is deliberately NOT
  like them, per the XACA-0340 canonical-source rule and this ticket's own
  mandate: it lives here, in dev-team, as the single source of truth, and is
  mirrored to the tap by an explicit `sync_file` line in sync-tap.sh. A
  future reader who notices the inconsistency with its directory-mates
  should not "correct" it by deleting the sync_file entry or moving this
  file tap-side-only — that would silently detach it from XACA-0340 and let
  the next tap-only edit revert on the next forward sync. The shared
  DESTINATION directory (share/templates/kanban/) is correct because this
  template is rendered by the same shared renderer those siblings use; only
  the PROVENANCE differs.

  ── TWO HARD REQUIREMENTS, BOTH VERIFIED — DO NOT "MODERNIZE" ───────────

  1. /bin/bash, NEVER /bin/zsh or a shebang-only invocation.
     Every <team>-startup.sh opens with a `cleanup_orphans` sweep:
       ps -eo pid,ppid,tty,comm | grep zsh | grep "??" | awk '$2 == 1 {print $1}' | xargs kill
     i.e. it kills every zsh process with ppid 1 and no controlling tty. A
     LaunchAgent-spawned process is EXACTLY that shape. If this plist ever
     invoked kb-host-ready.sh as zsh, the very first startup script the
     restore loop execs would kill its own parent mid-run — the lock step
     (§6 of the design) would then never be reached, silently, and on
     lock_after_login:true hosts that is a privacy hole, not a cosmetic bug.
     kb-host-ready.sh is itself #!/usr/bin/env bash for the same reason.

  2. PATH MUST include /opt/homebrew/bin.
     XACA-0713: launchd's inherited environment does not include Homebrew's
     bin dir, and that is where `tmux` lives on this fleet. Without it every
     tmux probe and every team restore invocation fails silently.

  ── TMUX_TMPDIR — DELIBERATE AND VERIFIED, NOT A LIMITATION ─────────────
  Set to the literal /tmp below. This is correct for this fleet and was
  verified live, not inferred.

  tmux resolves its socket dir as ${TMUX_TMPDIR:-/tmp}/tmux-$(id -u)
  (see kanban-helpers.sh). TMUX_TMPDIR is set NOWHERE in this repo's shell
  surface nor in the user's zsh startup files, so /tmp is the operative
  default for every interactively-started team. Confirmed against the
  running fleet: sockets live at /private/tmp/tmux-<uid>/ (academy, dns,
  finance-personal, legal-coparenting, medical, ...), and
  `tmux -L academy display-message -p '#{socket_path}'` reports
  /private/tmp/tmux-<uid>/academy.

  Pinning the literal here is therefore DEFENSIVE: it forces this launchd
  job onto the same socket directory the interactive sessions already use,
  closing exactly the divergence a launchd context could otherwise
  introduce. tests/test-xaca-0983-lcars-tmux-session-recreate.sh exists to
  simulate that very hazard ("a launchd agent whose $TMPDIR differs").

  DO NOT "fix" this by resolving `getconf DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR` inside
  kb-host-ready.sh. That would put this agent's sockets under
  /var/folders/<hash>/T/ while every interactive session stays on /tmp, so
  a restored team would be INVISIBLE to the user's own <team>-connect.sh —
  the precise failure this literal prevents. (kb-ttyd-bridge.sh's
  TMUX_TMPDIR placeholder resolves ${TMUX_TMPDIR:-/tmp}, which on this
  fleet evaluates to /tmp — the same value, reached by a longer route.)

  Genuinely open: per-host confirmation that M4Mini and M1Pro also resolve
  to /tmp. Neither sets TMUX_TMPDIR today, but that is a per-host fact and
  is carried into subitem 007's on-host checklist.

  ── StandardOutPath / StandardErrorPath ─────────────────────────────────
  Both point at the SAME file. This runs unattended (nobody is watching
  stdout at login), so a single chronologically-interleaved log is more
  useful post-mortem than two files that have to be read side by side to
  reconstruct the sequence — the same choice auto-upgrade-launchagent.template.plist
  makes for the same reason.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.aiteamforge.host-ready</string>
    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/bin/bash</string>
        <string>{{AITEAMFORGE_DIR}}/scripts/kb-host-ready.sh</string>
        <string>login</string>
    </array>
    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <true/>
    <key>KeepAlive</key>
    <false/>
    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>{{LOG_DIR}}/host-ready.log</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>{{LOG_DIR}}/host-ready.log</string>
    <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
    <dict>
        <key>PATH</key>
        <string>/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin</string>
        <key>HOME</key>
        <string>{{HOME_DIR}}</string>
        <key>AITEAMFORGE_DIR</key>
        <string>{{AITEAMFORGE_DIR}}</string>
        <key>TMUX_TMPDIR</key>
        <string>/tmp</string>
        <key>LANG</key>
        <string>en_US.UTF-8</string>
    </dict>
</dict>
</plist>
